# --- Runtime telemetry output ---
# The seeded/committed sample is kept (it is what docs/architecture.md
# screenshots and the Aegis contract test read); anything else written at
# runtime is not worth committing.
data/telemetry/*.jsonl
!data/telemetry/events.jsonl

# --- Publisher output ---
# The "pushed" PRs from backend/services/publisher.py land here. Generated
# artifacts, not source: regenerate with
# `python -m backend.scripts.run_remediation`.
data/published/

# --- Evidence harness (docs/evidence.md) ---
# Upstream repositories fetched on demand by backend/evidence/tier3.py, one
# shallow clone of two commits per advisory. Deliberately NOT committed:
# vendoring someone else's source imports their licence and their maintenance
# burden for no benefit, since the manifest in data/evidence/corpus.json already
# records every advisory and fix commit this project uses.
#
# Without this, `python scripts/evidence_report.py` leaves a few hundred megabytes
# of third-party git repositories in the working tree, and a reviewer cloning the
# repo would silently get all of them.
data/evidence/.cache/
